 R←⍙GitAdd ⍙RA;⍙CMD;⍙F;⍙PDIR;⍙T;⍙U;⍙V;⍙TEMP
⍝ Add a specified file to the current workspace's Git tracking.
⍝ The file must exist within the current workspace's parent
⍝ directory.  If the file name provided does not have an extension
⍝ it is assumed to be a reference to an APL object that
⍝
⍝ ]GIT Add /F=photo.jpg ⍝ Add a single file to this commit
⍝ ]GIT Add CMIOTA DTBV  ⍝ Add a two objects to this commit
⍝ ]Git Add .            ⍝ Add all files for this workspace to the commit
⍝
⍝ Note: Adding files (non-APL+Win objects) must be done separately from
⍝       adding objects (for now).
⍝
⍝ [TLDR: Tell git to track a file/object]

⍝ Get workspace path
 (⍙RA ⍙TEMP ⍙PDIR)←⍙RA ⍝ ⍙RA: Objects; ⍙TEMP: TempPath; ⍙PDIR: Parent dir
⍝ Update the workspace path's text files:
:If '.'≡⎕FIRST ⍙RA~' ' ⋄ ⍙T←⎕UCMD 'TOTXT' ⍝ All objects
:ElseIf ∨/⍙T←'/F='⍷⍙RA ⋄ ⍙RA←3↓(∨\⍙T)/⍙RA ⍝ Specific file
:Else ⍝ Specific object(s) {need to run ]TOTXT then git add the files}
   ⍙T←⎕UCMD 'TOTXT ',⍙RA,' /R'
  ⍝ Parse ]TOTXT result to determine created files:
  ⍝ ]TOTXT Foo Goo → '"C:\TEMP\Foo.aplwcv" created.',⎕TCNL,'"C:\TEMP\Goo.aplwcv" created.'
   ⍙U←∨/' created.'⍷⊃⍙V←(1,¯1↓⍙T∊⎕TCNL) ⎕PENCLOSE ⍙T
  ⍝ Drop the 'created.' portion of each result:
   ⍙V←¯10↓¨⍙U/⍙V
  ⍝ Take the file name from each result:
   ⍙RA←(1+-(⌽¨⍙V)⍳¨'\')↑¨⍙V
   ⍙RA←¯1↓⎕ENLIST ⍙RA,¨' '
:EndIf
 ⍙CMD←'git add ',⍙RA
⍝ Returns output from the ⎕CMD call:
 R←⍙TEMP ⍙COMMAND ⍙PDIR ⍙CMD
⍝ Deal with horrendous ⎕TCLF placement:
:if 0<⍴R ⋄ R←⊃((1,1↓⎕TCLF=R)⎕PENCLOSE R)~¨⎕TCLF ⋄ :endif